#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124232 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "be3d5a74-259e-58b9-948d-47ba7412ab08" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Rank of a Matrix Given the Number of Pivot Columns"}] :question/id #uuid "7cce27e9-e2b2-599c-9f4e-437caf1a23ae" :question/math-academy-id "e-5415" :question/problem "Let $A$ be a $4 \\times 7$ matrix that has $3$ **non-pivot** columns. Find $\\textrm{rank}(A)$." :question/worked-solution "We know that $\\textrm{rank}(A)$ is the number of pivot columns in $A$.\n\nSince $A$ has $7$ columns and $3$ of them are non-pivots, then the number of pivot columns in $A$ is\n$7-3=4$.\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\textrm{rank}(A)=4\n$$\n\n."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124233 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1d847ec9-c379-5013-ab77-a9b92dc8ca27" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Matrix With a Given Rank by Inspection"}] :question/id #uuid "a6a3db41-6033-537a-bc9d-03fde02dc869" :question/math-academy-id "e-5417" :question/problem "Which of the following matrices have a rank of $4$?\n\n$\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 7 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that a matrix of rank $4$ must have at least $4$ columns and at least $4$ rows.\nSo, we disregard the matrix $B$ since it has only $3$ rows.\n\nAlso, the matrix must have $4$ pivot columns. As we can see, the matrix $A$ has only $3$ pivot columns, while the matrix $C$ has exactly $4$ pivot columns. So,\n\n$$\n\\textrm{rank}(A)=3\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\textrm{rank}(C)=4\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$C$ only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124234 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7f5a44c9-16e5-55fb-a10f-15435a0a9a4c" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Rank of a Matrix Using Row Reduction"}] :question/id #uuid "b3e4eb01-0669-586b-a716-aef87d1c3580" :question/math-academy-id "e-5418" :question/problem "If $\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 5 \\\\ -4 & 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}$, find $\\textrm{rank}(A)$." :question/worked-solution "To find the rank of $A$, we first reduce it to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nA &= \\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 5 \\\\ -4 & 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{vmatrix}R_{3} &:=R_{3} + 2R_{1} \\\\ ∼\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 6 & 5\\end{bmatrix} & R_{3}\\end{vmatrix}:=R_{3} + 6R_{2} \\\\\n&= ∼\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 35\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix above has $3$ pivot columns (or, alternatively, it has exactly $3$ non-zero rows).\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\textrm{rank}(A)=3\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124773 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "be3d5a74-259e-58b9-948d-47ba7412ab08" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Rank of a Matrix Given the Number of Pivot Columns"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8ea42d22-d3e9-55a8-a4ca-3f67bd7350be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121661} {:answer/id #uuid "15306175-270c-5d2a-843b-fc891d354d47" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121662} {:answer/id #uuid "1dfe5931-5b47-5cc5-a510-152173e1a78e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121663} {:answer/id #uuid "36016731-106b-5f60-9363-04e53d9956c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121664} {:answer/id #uuid "3c79df69-1f79-5c27-b2cc-918838b57a9d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121665}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1dfe5931-5b47-5cc5-a510-152173e1a78e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121663} :answer-field/id #uuid "dd5c06ae-0b9d-533f-bd64-fd10b4a15abc" :answer-field/key "selection" :ans